+# ngx.http
+
+`ngx.http` is available in HTTP and Stream Lua when nginx is built with internal HTTP client support.
+
+## request_uri
+
+```lua
+local res, err = ngx.http.request_uri("https://example.com/api", {
+    method = "POST",
+    headers = { ["Content-Type"] = "application/json" },
+    body = [[{"ready":true}]],
+})
+```
+
+The call yields until the response is complete. On success, it returns a table with `status`, `headers`, and `body`. HTTP error status codes are returned in `status`. A request or transport failure returns `nil, err`.
+
+| Option | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `method` | Request method. Defaults to `GET`. |
+| `headers` | Request header table. Use an array of values for repeated fields. |
+| `body` | Request body string or chunk iterator. |
+| `query` | Query string or argument table. Replaces the query from the URL. |
+| `server` | Name of a configured internal `client;` server. Defaults to the shared `@client` server. |
+| `max_response_bytes` | Response body limit in bytes. Defaults to `16777216`. |
+
+Response header lookup is case-insensitive. Repeated response fields are returned as arrays in arrival order.
+
+The selected internal server sets the resolver, upstream connection, TLS, and timeout policy.
+An automatically created `@client` server inherits DNS settings from the `http` block.
+
+## request
+
+`ngx.http.request(url[, options])` returns the final response headers as soon as they are available. Read the response incrementally with `res.body_reader([size])`. Each call returns up to `size` bytes, `nil` at EOF, or `nil, err` if the transfer fails. Reads default to 16 KiB. Call `res:close()` when stopping before EOF. The reader belongs to the calling request and supports one pending read.
+
+```lua
+local res, err = ngx.http.request(url, { method = "POST", body = source_reader })
+if not res then
+    return nil, err
+end
+while true do
+    local chunk, err = res.body_reader(8192)
+    if not chunk then
+        return err == nil, err
+    end
+    local ok, err = sink(chunk)
+    if not ok then
+        res:close()
+        return nil, err
+    end
+end
+```
+
+Both request methods accept a body iterator. It receives a suggested chunk size and returns a non-empty string, `nil` at EOF, or `nil, err`. It may yield. Supply `Content-Length` when the request body length is known. Otherwise the client provides chunked framing. The selected location's `client_body_buffer_size` controls request body buffering. Its proxy buffering directives still apply.
+
+Streaming responses have no default total size limit. Set `max_response_bytes` to bound the entire response. A transfer error after headers is reported by the reader.
